.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH lrat-auth 1  lrat 
.SH NAME
lrat\-auth \- Manage the Linear API key
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlrat auth\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the Linear API key
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
lrat\-auth\-login(1)
Check an API key with Linear and store it in the configured keyring
.TP
lrat\-auth\-status(1)
Show where the API key comes from, and its workspace and viewer
.TP
lrat\-auth\-logout(1)
Delete the API key from the configured keyring
.SH EXTRA
Create a personal API key at https://linear.app/settings/account/security, then:
  lrat auth login                  paste the key at the prompt
  lrat auth login \-\-stdin          read it from a pipe, as in `pass linear | lrat auth login \-\-stdin`
  lrat auth login \-\-from\-keyring   copy it from an existing keyring entry (default linear/api\-key)
  lrat auth status                 check where the key comes from and which workspace it opens

LINEAR_API_KEY, when set, wins over the keyring. `[auth] store` in config.toml picks the keyring.
